--TEST--
a lens carries the command that lists what it counts: the uses for a reference count, the subclasses for a subclass count and the methods for an override lens, and a lens that counts nothing runs nothing, `rule:ide/five-features-are-one-reference-index`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {
    public function speak(): string { return ""; }
}
class Dog extends Animal {
    public function speak(): string { return "woof"; }
}
var $a = new Animal();
var $d = new Dog();
echo $d->speak();
--REQUEST--
codeLens
--EXPECT--
2:7 1 subclass -> case.nvs:5:7
2:7 2 references -> case.nvs:5:19, case.nvs:8:14
3:21 1 override -> case.nvs:6:21
3:21 no references
5:7 1 reference -> case.nvs:9:14
6:21 1 reference -> case.nvs:10:10
6:21 overrides Animal::speak -> case.nvs:3:21
